<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαμβλύνω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ</span>], fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῠνῶ</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blunt</i> or <i>dull the edge of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ξίφη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					40.24
				</span></i>
			 (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> mostly
			metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπίδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.82
				</span></i>
			 (tm.); of a person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεθηγμένον τοί μ᾽ οὐκ ἀπαμβλυνεῖς
					λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					715
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ λευκὰ τῶν τριχῶν ἀπαμβλύνει τὸν
					νοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					1.67
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάος ὄσσων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					4.525
				</span></i>
			; <i>tone down, take the edge off</i> a phrase, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				3.6.12
			</span></i>:—more freq. in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be blunted, lose its edge</i> or <i>force,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρη μὲν ἀπήμβλυνται, θυμὸς δὲ
					μενοινᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
					<u>Epigr.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Eleg.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γηράσκοντι συγγηράσκουσι αἱ φρένες καὶ
					ἐς τὰ πρήγματα πάντα ἀπαμβλύνονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.134
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαμβλυνθήσεται γνώμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					866
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμῖν -ύνεται ἡ δικαιοσύνη</span>”
				<i>is indistinctly seen,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					442d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			= foreg., <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				4.8.3
			</span></i> (s. v.l.).</div>
